1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,177
Lesson three.

2
00:00:01,177 --> 00:00:02,981
Clients do not know you.

3
00:00:02,981 --> 00:00:07,040
In less than one minute they decide if they trust you.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:11,400
Your profile and your portfolio must answer that question.

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:19,844
A strong profile has a clear photo, your real name, and one sentence that says what you do and for whom.

6
00:00:19,844 --> 00:00:22,087
Add your languages and tools.

7
00:00:22,087 --> 00:00:25,800
Keep it simple and honest, with no exaggeration.

8
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,500
No experience yet?

9
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,233
Create your own samples.

10
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:33,278
Choose three imaginary clients and do the work for them.

11
00:00:33,278 --> 00:00:36,600
Samples you made yourself are enough to start.

12
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,582
Your portfolio needs three to five of your best samples.

13
00:00:41,582 --> 00:00:44,855
For each one, write a short description.

14
00:00:44,855 --> 00:00:48,045
What was the goal, and what did you do.

15
00:00:48,045 --> 00:00:51,400
And make sure it opens easily on a phone.

16
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:59,497
Put it online in a free page or a simple website, and on your profile on freelance platforms.

17
00:00:59,497 --> 00:01:03,800
Keep one short link that you can send to any client.

18
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,205
Never fake it.

19
00:01:05,205 --> 00:01:10,231
Do not copy other people's work, and do not invent clients or reviews.

20
00:01:10,231 --> 00:01:15,400
Honesty builds long term trust, and platforms close accounts that cheat.

21
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:18,662
Show real work and explain it clearly.

22
00:01:18,662 --> 00:01:22,579
This week, create three samples and put them online.

23
00:01:22,579 --> 00:01:27,400
Next lesson: how to find your first client and write a proposal.

